On Sat, Sep 10, 2011 at 2:45 PM, Remo Dentato <rdentato@gmail.com> wrote:
> 2011/9/10 Jorge Llamb=EDas <jjllambias@gmail.com>:
>> On Sat, Sep 10, 2011 at 8:10 AM, Remo Dentato <rdentato@gmail.com> wrote=
:
>>> The CLL rule was that each brivla had to have a consonante cluster
>>> within the first five letters, not counting {y} and {'}, has this
>>> changed for fuhivla?
>>
>> Yes, I purposely dropped that requirement when writing the PEG
>> morphology, since it was arbitrary and not needed for anything.
>> There's no reason to allow ".a'a'alto" but forbid "pa'a'alto" due to
>> some strange counting of letters rule.
>
> It seems a very good thing to me. Still a fu'ivla must have a
> consonant cluster, right?

Yes, all brivla have a consonant cluster (if we count "CyC" as a
consonant cluster), and as Pierre pointed out, the second consonant in
a brivla is always part of a consonant cluster.

mu'o mi'e xorxes

